# Production requires confirmation

Eric's standing order: work only on local/preview unless he explicitly confirms production.

Before any of the following, stop and ask Eric in chat. Wait for a clear yes.

- Fukomo production: `fukomo.com`, PM2 `next-salon`, port `:3000`, nginx for that host, `/var/www/next-salon/.next` used by `next start`, `.env.production`
- Work production: `work.iseosalon.com`, systemd `:8001`, nginx for that host
- Restart, rebuild, deploy, patch compiled/build output, change production env, or edit files in a way that the live process will load
- Git commit/push that is meant to ship production

Local/preview only (no extra confirmation): Work `:3001`/`:8002`, Fukomo `:3002` / `next dev`.

Preview databases must stay separate from production:

- Fukomo preview: `salon_master_preview` + `*_preview` tenant DBs. Never `salon_master` / `next-salon` / live tenant URIs from `stores.dbUri`.
- Work preview: `work_preview`. Never `work_production`.
- One-way snapshot production → preview is allowed only to seed an isolated test DB. Never the reverse.

## Local test data never goes to production

For every bugfix and every new feature: **change scripts/code only**. Never copy, migrate, mongorestore, insert, upsert, or sync local/preview/trial/test data into production databases.

That includes appointments, customers, invoices, work orders, staff, services, packages, and any other documents created while testing on `:3001` / `:3002` / `:8002`. Production data stays production data. Local testing stays in `*_preview` / `work_preview`.

A report that production is broken is not permission to change it. Diagnose and propose the fix; apply on production only after Eric confirms. Code/script deploy still requires his yes. Data copy is never part of the deploy.
